# ~/.gitignore_global -- wired up via core.excludesfile in .gitconfig.
#
# ── Scope ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file applies to EVERY repository on the machine, including ones you do
# not own. So it contains only things that are a property of *this machine*:
# OS metadata, editor scratch files, and local tool state.
#
# Build output, dependency directories and language-specific artefacts are a
# property of the *project*, and belong in that project's own .gitignore. They
# are deliberately absent here.
#
# This file used to be a 1040-line gitignore.io dump covering 20+ languages,
# which globally ignored `pom.xml`, `Cargo.lock`, `bower.json`, `target/`,
# `build/`, `lib/`, `bin/`, `dist/` and `out/`. Files matching those would
# silently fail to be added, with `git add` reporting nothing at all. Do not
# add project-level patterns back here.

# ─── macOS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.TemporaryItems
.VolumeIcon.icns
.DocumentRevisions-V100

# ─── Linux ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.directory
.Trash-*
.fuse_hidden*
.nfs*

# ─── Windows (shared drives, colleagues' repos) ───────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ─── Vim / Neovim ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
.netrwhist
Session.vim

# ─── Emacs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# ─── JetBrains and VS Code ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Personal editor state. Projects that deliberately share editor settings
# should un-ignore them locally with a negation in their own .gitignore,
# e.g. `!.vscode/extensions.json`.
.idea/
.vscode/

# ─── Local tool state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.direnv/
.claude/settings.local.json
